I've never seen it written down anywhere. No one ever said: "Be" — that was the most important thing, and then they added all kinds of explanations about what to be in this way or another fashion — which is absolutely wrong!
It's not your state of mind, it doesn't depend upon Being; but once you are being yourself... that automatically gives a great impetus and power. That happens when one begins to realize the abysmal lack of "being" in their own life — a void which has been filled with all sorts of rubbish: it's really empty down there if you explore, but we don't have time for that.
A human being who is not yet "being" will always be unhappy;

